---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Dates: only years Amaan has given. "After matric" stands in where the year is not confirmed.
---
<Base
  title="My story | Amaan Omar"
  description="How a self-taught developer from Cape Town went from rebuilding his father's burnt-down shop to co-founding QuickLaunch and building with AI."
>
  <div class="container page-head story-head">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>My story</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I taught myself to code, rebuilt my father's fabric store after a fire, and co-founded QuickLaunch
        with Marcel Manikum. This is the road here, oldest first.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="placeholder arch story-photo" role="img" aria-label="Photo placeholder">
      Photo placeholder<br />Amaan at a table, 4:5
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="container story-list" aria-label="The road here">
    <ol class="changelog">
      <li>
        <time>Grade 6</time>
        <div>
          <h3>I started coding</h3>
          <p>
            I found an online course and learned a little C, C++ and C#, because I wanted to make video games.
            By grade 10 I was building small games and levels of my own.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2021">2021</time>
        <div>
          <h3>Rebuilt my father's fabric store</h3>
          <p>
            During covid I helped out in my father's fabric store. At the start of 2021, my matric year, the store
            burnt down and we lost all our income. I spent most of that year rebuilding it with him. During the
            June exams I was drilling shelves. We cut up the burnt shelving and reshaped it into tables, shelves
            and racks for the new shop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time>After matric</time>
        <div>
          <h3>Leaned on code</h3>
          <p>
            I left home at 18. I had a little programming and not much else, so I decided to lean on it and
            pursue it full time.
          </p>
          <p>
            I got a job at Ocean Basket after a lot of applications. On night shifts I coded in the morning, and
            on day shifts I coded at night. I was struggling, and they let me go. After that I worked about six
            months at a friend's parents' butter factory, still coding.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {/* [CONFIRM] "Gifties" (his spelling) vs "Giftees" (old site, giftees.net). */}
      <li>
        <time datetime="2023">2023</time>
        <div>
          <h3>A year at IDM, and freelancing at night</h3>
          <p>
            Then I spent a year at IDM in Cape Town, working on the marketing funnel and the tracking on landing
            pages. I got in by doing a project for the dev team manager. For six months there was no work for me,
            only "it's coming", and that killed my drive for the company. I didn't like corporate life, and it was
            still the best way I had to get experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            At the same time I was freelancing. I'd catch the bus at 6:30am, get home at 7pm, and work on Gifties,
            an international gifting platform built on Bubble, from 7 to 10pm. I had clients in Amsterdam, the US
            and Dubai. I saved up, and at the end of 2023 I quit to freelance full time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {/* [CONFIRM] R100,000 a month is revenue. */}
      <li>
        <time datetime="2024-05">May 2024</time>
        <div>
          <h3>Started CreatorConnect</h3>
          <p>
            In May 2024 I started my own company, CreatorConnect: a dashboard for UGC marketing agencies to track
            TikTok view counts, because there was no software for it. I built it very quickly. For a few months it
            reached R100,000 a month, about $25,000 in total. Then I burnt out and stopped.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2025">2025</time>
        <div>
          <h3>A low point, then QuickLaunch</h3>
          <p>At the start of 2025 I hit a low point.</p>
          <p>
            Then I decided to give business another shot and started QuickLaunch. I knew I needed a co-founder, so
            I went to every workshop and networking event I could. I met Marcel Manikum at one of them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {/* [CONFIRM] Jasiri wording; "technical side" vs "CTO". */}
      <li class="now">
        <time>Now</time>
        <div>
          <h3>QuickLaunch and Onnu</h3>
          <p>
            Today Marcel and I run QuickLaunch together. He's our CEO and I lead the technical side. QuickLaunch is
            part of Jasiri Talent Investor, Cohort 2 South Africa, and that's where I designed and built Onnu, our
            AI code-audit product.
          </p>
          <p>
            My work now is making AI build software reliably. I design the harnesses and guardrails that let AI
            write code safely, and the memory and context systems that keep AI agents accurate on large, real
            codebases. I also advise African startups and ventures on building with AI.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    {/*
      FAITH LINE: AWAITING AMAAN'S APPROVAL.
      Not rendered. Uncomment only once Amaan approves this wording
      (or replace it with his own sentence). Told as his values only; no comparison with any other faith.
      <p>
        I'm a Christian, and I want to be open about it. My faith shapes how I run my business, how I think,
        the decisions I make, how I live and the values I hold. It's part of everything I do.
      </p>
    */}
  </section>

  <div class="container"><div class="table-bar center" role="separator"></div></div>

  <section class="container prose story-close">
    <p>
      I never got a degree. Everything I know I learned by building things, breaking them and fixing them.
      If you're building with AI in Africa, I'd like to hear what you're working on.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a></div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .story-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 18rem; gap: var(--space-4); align-items: end; }
  .story-photo { width: 100%; }
  .story-close { padding-bottom: var(--space-5); text-align: center; margin-inline: auto; }
  .story-close .btn-row { justify-content: center; }
  .changelog p + p { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .story-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .story-photo { max-width: 14rem; grid-row: 1; }
  }
</style>
